# A flat node_modules, the way npm builds one.
#
# pnpm's default is an isolated store where each package sees only its own declared
# dependencies, which is stricter and generally better. It broke the Playwright suite:
# every spec loaded, and `test.describe` threw "Playwright Test did not expect
# test.describe() to be called here" — the runner and the spec files were holding two
# different instances of `@playwright/test`, because Playwright's own ESM loader resolves
# through a different path than `require.resolve` does under the isolated layout. All 31
# browser tests went to "No tests found" with nothing in the app changed.
#
# This repo was written and tested against npm's flat tree, so hoisting reproduces the
# layout everything here already assumes rather than chasing the strict-mode fallout
# through every tool. It is a deliberate step back from pnpm's better default, taken
# because the alternative was a green unit suite and a browser suite that silently ran
# zero tests — which is the worst of the available outcomes.
node-linker=hoisted
